* \L of a macro argument with '@' that a macro passes on to one using \L (Pm @O, Pm's body Tm \1):
* each '@' counts 1, as r68 counts it. r68togas writes '@' as _at_ (gas takes no '@' in names),
* and r68L counted that 4: @O was 5 long (move.l, not move.w). r68L now counts _at_ as 1 where
* the source had an '@' renamed.
* expect text: 3afc404f 3afc3a23 3afc4142 3afc4f40 3afc4040 2afc00784079 4e71
Tm macro
 ifgt \L1-1
 ifgt \L1-2
 move.l #'\1',(a5)+
 else
 move.w #'\1',(a5)+
 endc
 endc
 endm
Pm macro
 Tm \1
 endm
 psect mlat,0,0,0,0,0
 Pm @O
 Pm :#
 Pm AB
 Pm O@
 Pm @@
 Pm x@y
 ends
